{"content":"Fixed — the guest-controlled ref is now single-quoted and shell-escaped.

```js
var ghostRef = String(ticket.branch || '').replace(/'/g, "'\\''");
// …
' --ref \'' + ghostRef + '\''
```

So `ai/g'h-757;touch /tmp/pwn` dispatches as `--ref 'ai/g'\''h-757;touch /tmp/pwn'` — embedded quotes escaped, metacharacters inside single quotes.

Regression coverage: the IT-2 suite's `guest-controlled branch with shell metacharacters/quote` test asserts the exact escaped command string, and the happy-path IT-2 test pins the plain quoted form (`--ref 'ai/gh-757'`).

The pre-existing dispatch sites in this file share the older unquoted pattern — as the thread notes, that is consistency, not a new deviation; a follow-up to harden those the same way is worth tracking separately (they fire on machine-authored paths, not this guest-triggered one).
